00:29:37.240 --> 00:29:41.570
runner to essentially
say, hello, world.

00:29:41.570 --> 00:29:45.210
What we do here is we
define some function.

00:29:45.210 --> 00:29:47.600
It's going to end
up posting a message

00:29:47.600 --> 00:29:51.230
to some webhook on Slack, which,
if the internet keeps working,

00:29:51.230 --> 00:29:54.930
I'll start to see
notifications on my desktop.

00:29:54.930 --> 00:29:58.560
I go ahead and create that
function, give it a name,

00:29:58.560 --> 00:30:01.142
give it some Docker
image that runs,

00:30:01.142 --> 00:30:02.600
how much memory
