00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:05.210
This is kind of similar to
like a Cloud Function-like

00:30:05.210 --> 00:30:08.540
functionality,
serverless application.

00:30:08.540 --> 00:30:10.760
And I'm just going to run this.

00:30:10.760 --> 00:30:13.280
And I do that.

00:30:13.280 --> 00:30:19.500
And I can monitor what's going
on through this interface here.

00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:23.700
So we see that there's
10 pending messages here.

00:30:23.700 --> 00:30:26.270
So as that goes out
within Kubernetes,

00:30:26.270 --> 00:30:29.210
this is now finding
appropriate resources

00:30:29.210 --> 00:30:32.522
to place those workloads,
spin up those containers.

00:30:32.522 --> 00:30:33.980
And you can see
that we're starting

00:30:33.980 --> 00:30:37.730
to get Slack messages
saying, hello one, hello two.

00:30:37.730 --> 00:30:39.125
So that's all seeming to work.

00:30:42.290 --> 00:30:44.330
We can attach a webhook
to that task, where

00:30:44.330 --> 00:30:48.470
I post a message saying
like, what's next?

00:30:48.470 --> 00:30:50.630
And eventually,
