00:31:39.740 --> 00:31:42.230
and applies it to a
set of other images.

00:31:42.230 --> 00:31:44.750
So I was like, OK, that would
be pretty cool if we could

00:31:44.750 --> 00:31:48.482
pull this off during the demo.

00:31:48.482 --> 00:31:49.690
So we'll see if we can do it.

00:31:49.690 --> 00:31:53.150
So I essentially just copy and
pasted this whole workflow here

00:31:53.150 --> 00:31:58.220
from Keras and modified it a bit
so that what's going to happen

00:31:58.220 --> 00:31:59.180
is--

00:31:59.180 --> 00:32:06.150
let's see-- I'm going to take
